#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082913 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97802ae1-4976-5fdf-bbe1-bcd001d5e53a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given the First Term and Common Ratio"}] :question/id #uuid "2cd68908-78fc-56a2-9304-2aa5db4176c1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4190" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $-3$ and the common ratio is $2?$" :question/worked-solution "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\nS_N =\\dfrac{a_1(1-r^N)}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, $a_1= -3$ and $r = 2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{-3(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3)}{(-1)}(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =3(1-{2}^{N}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082914 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c17552f7-0720-5e45-9c79-7db73e332045" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given the First Few Terms"}] :question/id #uuid "45d0d5b6-71a3-5b09-a10f-1e4a62ed287a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4191" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of the geometric series $2+8+32+\\cdots \\: ?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{2} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{a_1 (1-r^N) }{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, $a_1=2$ and $r=4.$ Substituting these values into the formula for $S_N$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-{4}^{N})}{(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({4}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082915 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd32a853-e0ec-5d56-bd6b-1c2e0e3249f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given an Arbitrary Term and the Common Ratio"}] :question/id #uuid "10909636-a083-5a1c-bf88-f1334ef69666" :question/math-academy-id "e-4192" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $3$rd term is $18$ and the common ratio is $3?$" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine $a_1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 18 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{(3-1)} \\\\ 18 & =9{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{a_1 (1-r^N) }{1-r}\t.\n$$\n\nIn this case, $a_1=2$ and $r=3.$ Substituting our values into the formula for $S_N$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{2(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{2}(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & ={3}^{N}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97802ae1-4976-5fdf-bbe1-bcd001d5e53a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given the First Term and Common Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac5aa50-0c14-5498-9e9d-13edf124dc35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}({3}^{-N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328442} {:answer/id #uuid "a41f66c9-f9cd-5cb9-b21e-e7610d1c4a3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({4}^{-N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328443} {:answer/id #uuid "59e7aeff-cb57-53a1-a8aa-f73272eaa46e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}({4}^{-N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328444} {:answer/id #uuid "f37b9806-5c64-5cdf-84b2-357f8c4c475e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4({4}^{-N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328445} {:answer/id #uuid "133396cc-2531-5640-918a-487469d5bfbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3({3}^{-N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f37b9806-5c64-5cdf-84b2-357f8c4c475e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4({4}^{-N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328445} :answer-field/id #uuid "90f80dc0-083f-50e5-882c-e4c135b4d07c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a880b7a-8ca5-52a7-8783-3b205cea8268" :question/math-academy-id "q-110166" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $-3$ and the common ratio is $\\frac{1}{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=-3$ and $r=\\frac{1}{4}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{-3[1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}]}{(1-\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3[1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}]}{(\\frac{3}{4})} \\\\  & =-4[1-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}] \\\\  & =4[{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{N}-1] \\\\  & =4({4}^{-N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c17552f7-0720-5e45-9c79-7db73e332045" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given the First Few Terms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbb37495-c2dc-5fa0-b7c4-528abeffffc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({2}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328449} {:answer/id #uuid "d536d512-425a-57e5-a670-52b6cfce2756" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({4}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328450} {:answer/id #uuid "e8d97da8-22f6-5751-b400-5971c10b7bd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(1-{4}^{N})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328451} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d3c89d-620a-5cbf-aa46-8e2359a02da4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4({2}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328452} {:answer/id #uuid "304d7466-1c90-500a-b921-05d10b3ed4f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(1-{2}^{N})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9d3c89d-620a-5cbf-aa46-8e2359a02da4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4({2}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328452} :answer-field/id #uuid "07669529-00b9-5a8e-b0b8-8ccb8fd15785" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d39d6ffc-a04a-5e56-a39a-c11a40fa23e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-110180" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $4+8+16+\\,⋯?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=4$ and $r=2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{4(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =-4(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =4({2}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328454 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c17552f7-0720-5e45-9c79-7db73e332045" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given the First Few Terms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dfa61f3-c6e0-57a5-b9f5-2123aa077f4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}(6^N+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328456} {:answer/id #uuid "26f1bf3c-196e-5832-88b4-c1f6d2d4909b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}(6^N-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26f1bf3c-196e-5832-88b4-c1f6d2d4909b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}(6^N-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328457} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbffc279-c38d-5246-a3ed-9f0c6e17c348" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328455}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0e583e3c-68ff-5a26-a404-3d96c2b20a2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-270557" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $7+42+252+\\,⋯?$ Express your answer as a function of $N.$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{42}{7} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=7$ and $r=6.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{7(1-{6}^{N})}{1-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{7(1-{6}^{N})}{(-5)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{5}(1-{6}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}({6}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328458 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97802ae1-4976-5fdf-bbe1-bcd001d5e53a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given the First Term and Common Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93d305e8-f5f1-5174-97d7-8104d428e529"