ef 17592186328465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3041515-0f9d-5c86-8a43-ef97d983f10b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5(2^N-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328464} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0793865-dda4-58f5-944f-71bf872b9b33" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2eb0daf-a508-5ea3-8ad9-3a68146465db" :question/math-academy-id "q-276481" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $5+10+20+⋯?$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=5$ and $r=2.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{5(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =-5(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =5({2}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328466 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c17552f7-0720-5e45-9c79-7db73e332045" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given the First Few Terms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4de5897-78b7-52f8-98fa-d0fbf3194f0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(3^N-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4de5897-78b7-52f8-98fa-d0fbf3194f0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(3^N-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328468} :answer-field/id #uuid "73b662cd-3dcc-5b05-8e2e-79d93866cd68" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cac3a52a-4ec7-51c8-87df-4a1dd61e0e9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-276482" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $6+18+54+⋯?$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{6} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=6$ and $r=3.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{6(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{2}(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & =3({3}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328469 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd32a853-e0ec-5d56-bd6b-1c2e0e3249f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given an Arbitrary Term and the Common Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79b80505-54ad-53ca-a7c8-0232754ec326" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(3^N+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328471} {:answer/id #uuid "2834e98b-10d6-5b2f-83e2-8210fde5b77f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(3^N-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2834e98b-10d6-5b2f-83e2-8210fde5b77f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(3^N-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328472} :answer-field/id #uuid "c36a8833-b87c-501a-820d-f54641a91a20" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2a03e1d4-3899-53ba-b621-6a814f66aa1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-276485" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $4$th term is $324$ and the common ratio is $3?$ Express your answer as a function of $N,$ making sure you use a capital letter $(N,$ not $n).$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 324 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 324 & =27{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=12$ and $r=3.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{12(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{12(1-{3}^{N})}{(-2)} \\\\  & =-6(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & =6({3}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328473 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97802ae1-4976-5fdf-bbe1-bcd001d5e53a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given the First Term and Common Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ebaea0f-9d95-5a80-889d-dfb04816738d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(6^N-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ebaea0f-9d95-5a80-889d-dfb04816738d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(6^N-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328475} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf0f97c8-81c5-51fd-b0a2-c3bcec9b75c0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3d35ba27-9946-5131-9463-0bd7e5dff14c" :question/math-academy-id "q-276993" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the first term is $15$ and the common ratio is $6?$ Express your answer as a function of $N,$ making sure you use a capital letter $(N,$ not $n).$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=15$ and $r=6.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{15(1-{6}^{N})}{1-6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{5}(1-{6}^{N}) \\\\  & =3({6}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd32a853-e0ec-5d56-bd6b-1c2e0e3249f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given an Arbitrary Term and the Common Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d42e3474-809a-50b4-84bd-071d38310aba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8(2^N-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d42e3474-809a-50b4-84bd-071d38310aba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8(2^N-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328478} :answer-field/id #uuid "632de4db-342a-5a66-9c88-aa31c1466dc3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cad8ab82-cf5f-5932-b397-22a270d16a6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-277872" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $7$th term is $512$ and the common ratio is $2?$ Express your answer as a function of $N,$ making sure you use a capital letter $(N,$ not $n).$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 512 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {2}^{(7-1)} \\\\ 512 & =64{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=8$ and $r=2.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{8(1-{2}^{N})}{1-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8(1-{2}^{N})}{(-1)} \\\\  & =-8(1-{2}^{N}) \\\\  & =8({2}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "97802ae1-4976-5fdf-bbe1-bcd001d5e53a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Sum of a Geometric Series Given the First Term and Common Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1da1c7b-a845-5120-8f25-a1337d02489c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}(1-{3}^{N})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328481} {:answer/id #uuid "53fb81d2-eab2-5e8a-acd5-99bd7896e124" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{14}({15}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328482} {:answer/id #uuid "fbee3794-90b6-53b4-b8f3-0b4d142f4fbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}({15}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328483} {:answer/id #uuid "7eac3eb6-c061-54d6-a4cf-7f78fe261e17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}(1-{15}^{N})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328484} {:answer/id #uuid "67123802-2886-5df8-87f9-70970f5ce3cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}({3}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53fb81d2-eab2-5e8a-acd5-99bd7896e124" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{14}({15}^{N}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328482} :answer-field/id #uuid 